NAME
       run-parts - run every program in a directory

SYNOPSIS
       run-parts DIRECTORY

DESCRIPTION
       run-parts runs each executable file in DIRECTORY, one after the other,
       in alphabetical order. cron uses it for the directories
       /etc/cron.hourly, /etc/cron.daily, /etc/cron.weekly and
       /etc/cron.monthly: a script dropped there (and made executable with
       chmod +x) runs at that rhythm. Files that are not executable are
       skipped.

EXAMPLES
       Run the daily jobs now, to test a new script:

           run-parts /etc/cron.daily

SEE ALSO
       crontab(5), crond(8), anacron(8)
